From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): combine queued messages into one

When several messages wait behind a running turn, steering sends each one
as its own message, so the agent gets several partial steers instead of one
combined instruction.

When two or more adjacent queued messages can merge, the queue strip's
header now offers Combine: their texts are joined by a blank line and their
attachments concatenated, in queue order, in the first message's place.
Where rows can be steered, Send all combines and then steers the queue. Side
chats get the same actions.

Messages that have to be sent as they are stay separate and in place: `!`
shell commands; `/`-led commands, skills and paths, which the harness reads
as the first text; Codex `$` skills; failed sends the server may already
hold; and item-comment messages, whose drafts are tracked by the exact text
they were sent with. Nothing moves across such a message, so the runs on
either side combine separately; a change of agent also starts a new run.
The merge is a pure function over the queued messages, so it can move to
the server with the queue.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/queue-combine; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
